<title>USA: Raines expects Clinton budget to be well-received.</title>
<headline>Raines expects Clinton budget to be well-received.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House Budget Director Franklin Raines said Monday he expects President Clinton's budget, which will be unveiled Thursday, to be well-received in Congress.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a good budget, it meets the president's stated goal of balancing by 2002,&quot; Raines told reporters at the U.S. Government Printing Office.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it will be a budget that will be well-received,&quot; because it achieves balance by 2002, he said.</p>
</text>
